From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: build without warnings

- kbuild has not read EXTRA_CFLAGS for years. The fdrv Makefile's
  -Wno-implicit-fallthrough and USER_EXTRA_CFLAGS (never set for this
  driver) were dead. The vendor shares global functions between files
  without header declarations, so both modules now build with
  -Wno-missing-prototypes -Wno-missing-declarations (102 warnings).
- rwnx_main.c: the kernel builds with -Wimplicit-fallthrough=5, which
  ignores "/* fall-through */" comments; use the fallthrough keyword.
- aic8800d80{,x2}_compat.c: a "defined" produced by a macro expansion is
  undefined in #if; IS_ENABLED() gives the same 0 or 1.
- rwnx_msg_tx.c: the length check that 0001 adds was indented with
  spaces, so the next statement looked guarded by it.

No functional change.

diff --git a/aic8800_bsp/Makefile b/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
index 2a0049a..11894ef 100644
--- a/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
+++ b/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+# Vendor functions are shared between files without header declarations.
+ccflags-y += -Wno-missing-prototypes -Wno-missing-declarations
 CONFIG_SDIO_SUPPORT := y
 CONFIG_SDIO_PWRCTRL := n
 #CONFIG_AIC_FW_PATH = "/vendor/etc/firmware"
